From 8c9705ee5fc3e5ac0dae34c0e0c3732cba84fcc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:07:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): Explain G-code option, explain() PRELUDE helper,
 manifest and refusal

Adds the opt-in Explain G-code post option (PostOptions.explain, per
document and per setup, through the existing undoable post-options
commands; the project file writes an `explain` key only when on). The
script engine loads an explain() helper after the PRELUDE and arms it
only when the option is on and the post's manifest states
`explains = "paren" | "semi"` (optional `commentMax`, 8..=255, default
60). Unarmed, explain() returns "", so Explain-off output is unchanged.
Explain on with a post that states no form is refused by the post's
name before any hook runs.

Fixes #1386

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
